<figure class="ai-whole-stack not-prose" aria-labelledby="ai-whole-stack-title">
  <header>
    <p>From output to consequence</p>
    <h2 id="ai-whole-stack-title">The machine is the whole stack</h2>
  </header>

  <ol>
    <li>
      <span>01</span>
      <div>
        <strong>Base model and weights</strong>
        <p>A trained statistical system that can generalize, infer, fail, and surprise its builders.</p>
      </div>
    </li>
    <li>
      <span>02</span>
      <div>
        <strong>Post-training and system instructions</strong>
        <p>The behavior the developer rewards, discourages, or places above the user’s request.</p>
      </div>
    </li>
    <li>
      <span>03</span>
      <div>
        <strong>Classifiers, memory, and product rules</strong>
        <p>Hidden checks, retrieved context, account settings, regions, and the interface around the model.</p>
      </div>
    </li>
    <li>
      <span>04</span>
      <div>
        <strong>Tools, credentials, and permissions</strong>
        <p>The files, networks, databases, services, passwords, and machines the system can reach.</p>
      </div>
    </li>
    <li>
      <span>05</span>
      <div>
        <strong>Operator and customer</strong>
        <p>The person or organization choosing the objective, judging the output, and deciding whether to act.</p>
      </div>
    </li>
    <li>
      <span>06</span>
      <div>
        <strong>Company, contract, government, and law</strong>
        <p>The institution that supplies money, policy, authority, incentives, targets, and consequences.</p>
      </div>
    </li>
    <li>
      <span>07</span>
      <div>
        <strong>Real-world effect</strong>
        <p>A paragraph, a picture, a changed file, an account lock, an alert, a purchase, a search, or a strike.</p>
      </div>
    </li>
  </ol>

  <figcaption>
    A model can produce a bad idea. The surrounding system gives the idea a password, a target, a budget, and permission to proceed.
  </figcaption>
</figure>

